From 3ef8bed09161bb182bbc3ade2f0eb1c4a8cb3222 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:31:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Tell Cartouche where its actions stopped and why

LiveContainer passes back to Cartouche only the text of an action's
error, which Cartouche shows the player and never sends: its
measurements knew that signing in failed, not where nor why.

Sign In to Cartouche, Refresh All Apps and Update Cartouche now leave
Cartouche, in the keychain item cartouche.outcome, how they ended: the
step reached (the sign-in's own steps, or the last operation started,
which every operation notes as it starts), how far it got, how long it
took, and the error as names and numbers: its family and case, its
domains and codes, Apple's code, the HTTP status, the URL error's code
and what the server it could not reach is (Apple, SideStore, GitHub,
the device), never its address. The sign-in also notes whether Apple
asked for a verification code and how, how many certificates the
account has and whether this SideStore holds one. Never the error's
words, an Apple ID, a team, a device or a path.
